# House rule 6 is about code, and this file is where "code" is drawn.
#
# The line is drawn by subtraction, so that it stays drawn as the tree grows:
# the formatter owns every file it can parse, and one leaves that scope only by
# appearing below with the reason it left — another gate already judges it, or
# reformatting it would change what it says. A kind of file this tree does not
# have yet is in scope on the day it arrives; an inventory of the kinds in
# scope would be wrong on that day instead.
#
#   *.md               .chug/tasks/doc-lint.sh owns markdown well-formedness,
#                      and this tree's prose is hand-wrapped. A reflow would
#                      produce a diff on every file, touching every line, for
#                      no reader's benefit.
#   .chug/             shell, and .chug/tasks/check-shell-quoting.sh is what
#                      judges it.
#   .githooks/         the same shell, under the same gate.
#   model/             Quint, which Prettier does not parse.
#   .claude/           not this tree's file to format.
#   package-lock.json  npm writes it, in npm's format.
#
# A file this list covers is not unformatted; it is judged by whatever the line
# beside it names. Everything else Prettier parses, Prettier formats.

# Both forms, for .gitignore's reason and after the same failure: the
# trailing-slash form matches a directory only, so a SYMLINK named
# node_modules walks straight past it. A suite fixture links one in rather
# than installing a second copy, and the formatter then walked the whole real
# tree on every case.
node_modules
node_modules/

*.md
.chug/
.githooks/
model/
.claude/
package-lock.json
